<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S3.SS2.SSS2.Px1" title="In 3.2.2 The Iterative Self-improvement Stage ‣ 3.2 Ablation Studies and Observations ‣ 3 Experiments ‣ POINTS-Reader: Distillation-Free Adaptation of Vision-Language Models for Document Conversion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">These filtering strategies effectively increase the quality of the data.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S3.SS2.SSS2.Px2" title="In 3.2.2 The Iterative Self-improvement Stage ‣ 3.2 Ablation Studies and Observations ‣ 3 Experiments ‣ POINTS-Reader: Distillation-Free Adaptation of Vision-Language Models for Document Conversion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">The F1-score threshold plays a crucial role in ensuring the quality of training data.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S3.SS2.SSS2.Px3" title="In 3.2.2 The Iterative Self-improvement Stage ‣ 3.2 Ablation Studies and Observations ‣ 3 Experiments ‣ POINTS-Reader: Distillation-Free Adaptation of Vision-Language Models for Document Conversion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">We observe improved quality of the real-world data to train our model.</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S3.SS3" title="In 3 Experiments ‣ POINTS-Reader: Distillation-Free Adaptation of Vision-Language Models for Document Conversion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">3.3 </span>Comparison with Other Models</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
